 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance authorizing The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to accept new public water and sanitary sewer mains, fire hydrant assemblies, sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for three properties located on Lawrence Avenue and Bellefield Avenue, also known as Moda Vista (MWS Project Nos. 26-WL-15 and 26-SL-36 and Proposal No. 2026M-087ES-001).\n..body\nWHEREAS, the acceptance of approximately 5,453 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 3,224 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 1,114 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), nine fire hydrant assemblies, 33 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for three properties located on Lawrence Avenue (unnumbered) and Bellefield Avenue (unnumbered), also known as Moda Vista, is needed to construct Project Nos. 26-WL-15 and 26-SL-36; and,\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Planning Commission approved mandatory referral No. 2026M087ES-001 on September 17, 2026, for the acceptance of said water and sanitary sewer mains, fire hydrant assemblies, sanitary sewer manholes and easements. \nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County is authorized to accept approximately 5,453 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 3,224 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 1,114 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), nine fire hydrant assemblies, 33 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for three properties located on Lawrence Avenue (unnumbered) and Bellefield Avenue (unnumbered), also known as Moda Vista, as shown on Exhibit 1, which is attached hereto and incorporated by reference:\nMap & Parcel: \t\t\t\tAddress:\n069120I00100CO\t\t\t\tLawrence Avenue (unnumbered)\n069120I00200CO\t\t\t\tLawrence Avenue (unnumbered)\n069120I00300CO\t\t\t\tBellefield Avenue (unnumbered)\nSection 2.\tThe Directors of Water and Sewerage Services and Public Property Administration are authorized to execute such documents as may be necessary and appropriate to carry out the acceptance authorized by this ordinance. \nSection 3.\tAmendments to this legislation shall be approved by resolution.\nSection 4.\tThis ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it. \n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis ordinance accepts approximately 5,453 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 3,224 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 1,114 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), nine fire hydrant assemblies, 33 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for three properties located on Lawrence Avenue (unnumbered) and Bellefield Avenue (unnumbered), also known as Moda Vista.\n\nThis ordinance has been approved by the Planning Commission. Future amendments to this ordinance may be approved by resolution.\n\nFiscal Note: This ordinance has no cost to Metro. Donated easements have no market value according to the Department of Water Services.\n\n"
